{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504428,"nonce":"iFNdd0XnzVTrKOuyUYRVFU1M450=","title":"No type implements either `EventRecorder` port, so the five `rule.*`/`enrichment.*` timeline types AC-16 requires can never be written","was":"**What is wrong.** `rules/service.EventRecorder` (`internal/rules/service/ports.go:130`) and `enrichment/service.EventRecorder` (`internal/enrichment/service/ports.go:142`) have **zero implementations anywhere in the tree**, production or test-adjacent-to-production. The container never supplies either: `internal/app/container.go:416-421` builds `rulesservice.New` with `Repo`, `Lookup`, `Clock`, `Logger` and no `Events:` key, and `:497-511` builds `enrichservice.New` with `Registry`, `Repo`, `Cache`, `Subjects`, `Notifier`, `Enqueuer`, `Clock`, `Logger` and no `Events:` key. Both fields are documented as optional, so both services start clean and both narrators return immediately, forever."}]}